+      the current token-candidate slate with the native DiffusionGemma logits and an executable-verifier
+      energy. The composed score for token t at position i is
+      logit_model(i,t) - lambda_energy * verifier_energy(partial_canvas with t inserted). Sampling/commit
+      uses the same low-entropy DiffusionGemma commit order after this reweighting; no post-hoc reranking
+      of completed samples is counted as guided diffusion."
+    - A NEW mitigation to consider for the guidance itself (per exp5172's SOTA-ingestion literature find):
+      EDLM (arXiv:2410.21357, ICLR 2025) documents a concrete, ~1.3x-overhead (not Nx) energy-injection
+      recipe for discrete diffusion denoising -- read it if the exp5173 formula above needs a concrete
+      implementation reference for the resampling/reweighting step.
+    - CIRCULARITY CONTROL (per CLAUDE.md's Circularity/Oracle-Distinctness Discipline -- exp5173 got
+      flagged CIRCULAR_MOAT_OVERCLAIM/MOAT_CLAIM_RIGOR for setting verifier_is_oracle=true while framing
+      results as gate-eligible): if the `verifier_energy` term in the guidance formula is computed by an
+      EXECUTABLE test-suite oracle (the same oracle that defines task correctness), set
+      `verifier_is_oracle: true` explicitly and frame any positive result as "execution-grounded
+      verification helps diffusion decoding" -- NOT as a moat-proven claim, and do NOT flip the
+      DiffusionGemma gate on this alone. If instead you use an oracle-DISTINCT energy (a learned/probe
+      signal, not the test oracle itself), set `verifier_is_oracle: false` and this result IS
+      gate-eligible. Decide and declare this BEFORE running any arm, not after seeing results.
+    - CONTROL ARM for intrinsic confidence (per exp5172's citation): VFScale (arXiv:2502.01989) -- an
+      intrinsic-confidence-only signal with no external verifier, to separate "guidance helps because it's
+      a verifier" from "guidance helps because any confidence signal would."
+    - TELEMETRY precondition (per exp5172's citation): commit-position telemetry (arXiv:2606.14620) --
