+  prompt: |
+    CONTEXT:
+    Repo at {project_root}, run on or after {date}. Hidden-state / internal-representation verifiers
+    (TrajSelector-style, arXiv:2510.16449) are the ONE sanctioned exception to `.474`'s PHASE D
+    external-text-scorer retirement -- an architecturally distinct mechanism class (scores the
+    generator's OWN hidden activations, not its generated text or logprobs). `.474`'s exp5178 pilot was
+    honest but underpowered and used a weak probe design. This task retries with the fixes exp5178's own
+    diagnosis implies are needed.
+
+    THE CORPUS: `results/experiment_mmlu_pro_verifier_candidate_pool.jsonl` (240 rows) is a REAL,
+    already-measured, headroom-CONFIRMED pool (`results/experiment_mmlu_pro_fresh_headroom_check.json`:
+    `oracle_at_k=0.350`, `sc_vote=0.075`, `headroom=0.275`, `headroom_ci95=[0.150,0.425]` -- clearly
+    excludes 0, adversarial_verify 0-flagged). Per arXiv:2512.02304's headroom-precondition formalism
+    (independently confirming PHASE D's own empirical lesson), a verifier can only conceivably beat
+    self-consistency where real headroom exists -- this corpus has it; exp5178's MuSR slice largely did
+    not (near-ceiling).
+
+    THE PROBE DESIGN (PHSV, arXiv:2504.05419 -- "Reasoning Models Know When They're Right: Probing Hidden
+    States for Self-Verification"): chunk reasoning traces at natural boundary markers ("wait",
+    "double-check", step transitions), extract last-token/last-layer hidden state at each chunk boundary,
+    train a small 2-layer MLP classifier on (hidden_state, correctness_label) pairs, reported AUROC
+    0.75-0.91 on comparable open-weight local models.
+
+    KNOWN EXTRACTION CONSTRAINT (do not silently ignore this): exp5178 found that
+    `llama_cpp.Llama(embedding=True, pooling_type=LAST).embed` -- the extraction path already validated in
+    this repo for `unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF` -- exposes ONLY the final-token, final-layer embedding
+    vector; llama.cpp does not expose per-layer hidden states or steering hooks. PHSV's chunk-boundary
+    recipe is compatible with final-layer extraction (it also uses last-token/last-layer as its primary
+    recipe), but the FEPoID (arXiv:2605.26366) layer-sweep finding ("intermediate layers often beat
+    final-layer") is NOT achievable through this extraction path without a heavier `transformers`-library
+    load (`output_hidden_states=True`) of the same model. Treat the layer-sweep as OPTIONAL/stretch: if
+    the `transformers` load path is straightforward given exp5182's DiffusionGemma device-placement work
+    this same milestone, attempt it; if not, proceed with final-layer-only (matching exp5178's and PHSV's
+    primary recipe) and note the limitation explicitly rather than silently omitting the comparison.
+
+    MANDATORY CONTROL ARMS (so a trained probe's extraction overhead has to earn its keep against
+    zero-training alternatives):
+    - Self-certainty (arXiv:2502.18581): a zero-training baseline from logit-distribution divergence from
+      uniform -- no hidden-state extraction at all.
+    - CLUE (arXiv:2510.01591): non-parametric hidden-state clustering, training-free (uses the same
+      extracted vectors as the trained probe, but no MLP fit).
+    - Tuned self-consistency (the baseline every verifier-moat claim in this project must beat).
+
+    This task doubles as the milestone's continuous-self-learning experiment (research-program.md
+    requires at least one per milestone): the probe is trained on the model's own accumulated
+    correct/incorrect experience over the 240-row pool, and per CLAUDE.md's Missing-Verifier Gap Logging
+    discipline, any residual failure mode (a candidate class the probe cannot discriminate) should be
+    logged to `ops/verifier_gaps.md` as a new or updated gap entry.
+
+    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
+    - results/experiment_5178_hidden_state_verifier_pilot_v474.json (the prior pilot's exact extraction
+      path, `hidden_state_access_metadata`, and probe design -- read to avoid repeating the same
+      naive-centroid mistake).
+    - results/experiment_mmlu_pro_fresh_headroom_check.json and
+      results/experiment_mmlu_pro_verifier_candidate_pool.jsonl (the target corpus).
+    - python/carnot/experiment_5178_hidden_state_verifier_pilot_v474.py (the extraction harness -- extend
+      with the chunk-boundary/MLP probe, do not rewrite the GGUF-loading plumbing).
+    - CLAUDE.md "Circularity / Oracle-Distinctness Discipline" (this MUST declare `verifier_is_oracle:
+      false` -- gold labels are for training/eval splits only, per exp5178's own correct precedent).
+
+    CONCRETE STEPS:
+    0. PRECONDITIONS: confirm the GGUF model is cached (per exp5178's `hidden_state_access_metadata.gguf_path`)
+       and the candidate pool file exists and has 240 rows. If either is missing, `blocked_<resource>`.
+    1. Extract hidden-state vectors for every candidate in the pool via the validated llama.cpp embedding
+       path (reuse exp5178's exact extraction call).
+    2. Split the pool into train/eval with NO leakage across the same question (k-fold or held-out by
+       question_id, matching the leakage-safe pattern the retired PHASE D program itself established for
+       D1's trained embedding verifier).
+    3. Train the PHSV-style 2-layer MLP probe on the training split.
+    4. Compute self-certainty and CLUE control-arm scores on the SAME eval split (no extra LLM calls
+       needed for self-certainty; CLUE reuses the already-extracted vectors).
+    5. Score all four methods (trained probe, self-certainty, CLUE, tuned self-consistency) on the eval
+       split's selection accuracy; compute paired bootstrap CI95 and McNemar p-value for probe-vs-SC and
+       probe-vs-each-control-arm.
+    6. If straightforward, attempt the FEPoID-style layer-sweep as a stretch goal via a `transformers`
+       library load; otherwise report final-layer-only and note the limitation.
+    7. Update `ops/verifier_gaps.md` with the residual failure-mode analysis (which candidate class, if
+       any, the probe cannot discriminate) per the Missing-Verifier Gap Logging discipline.
+
+    REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:
+      probe_accuracy:
+        value: float
+      self_certainty_accuracy:
+        value: float
+      clue_accuracy:
+        value: float
+      tuned_sc_accuracy:
+        value: float
+      probe_vs_sc_delta_ci95:
+        value: "[lo, hi]"
+      probe_vs_sc_mcnemar_p:
+        value: float
+      n_questions:
+        value: int
+        principle: "Must be materially larger than exp5178's n=6 -- this is the direct fix for the prior
+          pilot's underpowered sample."
+      layer_sweep_attempted:
+        value: bool
+      headroom_present:
+        value: true
+      verifier_is_oracle:
+        value: false
+        principle: "Gold labels are for training/eval splits only; must be false per the
+          Circularity/Oracle-Distinctness Discipline."
+      missing_verifier_gaps:
+        value: "residual failure-mode entries logged to ops/verifier_gaps.md"
+      random_seed:
+        value: int
+      reproducibility_checksum:
+        value: string
+      inference_substrate:
+        value: live_llm_embedding_extraction
+        principle: "Matches exp5178's corrected substrate declaration -- a single forward pass per
+          candidate for embedding extraction, not full autoregressive generation; 2.0s floor applies."
+      honest_verdict:
+        principle: "Must start with complete:/complete_/success:/success_, and state plainly whether the
+          trained probe beats tuned SC AND beats both zero-training control arms -- beating SC alone is
+          insufficient if a zero-training baseline (self-certainty or CLUE) does equally well."
+
+    Do not push. Do not modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
